<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05DK">Remark <span data-tag="05DK">4.8.8.3</span>.</a> In the situation of Definition <a data-tag="05DJ" href="/tag/05DJ">4.8.8.2</a>, we can assume without loss of generality that the functor $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is an isofibration (see Corollary <a data-tag="02VM" href="/tag/02VM">4.5.3.24</a>). Replacing $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ by the simplicial set $\operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n-1}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}/\operatorname{\mathcal{D}})}}$, we can further arrange that the isofibration $U$ is $(n-1)$-categorical (Proposition <a data-tag="05DC" href="/tag/05DC">4.8.6.24</a>). </p>
